   "displayId": "textTurn_exploreDataFromNL_1794700600000_closing",
   "textKind": "explain",
   "content": "**Nigeria has the widest gap of the 86 countries with recent surveys:** 89.8% of young people from the richest fifth of families finished upper secondary school, against 15.7% from the poorest fifth, a **74-point gap** (2021).\n\nLaos (71 points), Ghana (68 points), Lesotho (66 points) and Zambia (64 points) come next.\n\nThe dashboard sets the richest against the poorest for the widest gaps; the map beside it can switch between the gap and each group's rate. Each country's latest survey from 2018–2025. Source: UIS, November 2026 release; indicators CR.3.Q1, CR.3.Q5.",
   "parentNodeId": "file-completion_by_wealth.app.jsx",
